-- Spanish. The planner's fourth language, and the last one falling back.
--
-- Dan, 21 August 2026: "This is deployed - please take on Spanish now"
--
-- DATA, LIKE FRENCH WAS. German paid for the structure -- eighteen
-- standing invariants restated against violation counts, a coverage
-- counter that disagreed with an invariant about benchmark labels, four
-- tests using the untranslated language as their fixture. French
-- confirmed none of it recurred. Spanish confirms it again: 433 strings,
-- 31 benchmarks, 7 phases, and nothing structural to touch.
--
-- Spanish runs 14% longer than English -- the shortest of the three, under
-- German's 15% and French's 17% -- so the layout that survived German has
-- nothing new to survive here.
--
-- THE VOCABULARY IS THE SITE'S OWN, read out of i18n/es.json rather than
-- invented: mandato, fecha límite, país, cumplimiento, facturación
-- electrónica, reporte digital. Also costo rather than coste, and ola for
-- wave, because the auth panel added in 596 already says "olas de
-- cumplimiento" -- a reader crossing from the panel to the planner meets
-- the same word.
--
-- ONE DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE FROM THE TRACKER, recorded here rather than
-- found later as an inconsistency. The tracker's filters.nextClearanceDates
-- renders clearance as «compensación», which is settlement/clearing in the
-- financial sense and is not what a clearance regime is; a Spanish tax
-- professional reads it as the wrong thing. The planner keeps the industry
-- term clearance, as German and French do and as Spanish e-invoicing
-- literature does ("modelo de clearance"). The two pages disagree on
-- purpose, and the TRACKER string is the one worth revisiting. Not changed
-- here: it is one string on another page, and changing it is Dan's call
-- rather than a side effect of translating this one.
--
-- ZERO IS SINGULAR IN SPANISH as it is in French. Intl.PluralRules says so,
-- the page has selected on CLDR categories since 573, and roi-regression
-- asserts it -- no extra rows, only the knowledge that it is handled.
--
-- QUOTED SOURCE MATERIAL STAYS IN ENGLISH, as in German and French: the
-- citations quote HMRC, the ATO, APQC, Ardent and the OECD verbatim inside
-- &ldquo;&rdquo;, and the prose around them is what is translated.
--
-- BENCHMARK LABELS ARE THE EMPTY STRING. getRoiBenchmarks reads only hint
-- and citation; a standing invariant forbids a non-English label, and the
-- column is NOT NULL.
--
-- AND AFTER THIS, NO SUPPORTED LANGUAGE FALLS BACK. That is worth saying
-- out loud because a test depended on one doing so: roi-regression rendered
-- the complete-or-English notice by naming a real site language that had
-- not been translated yet. There is no such language now, and the honest
-- fix is a synthetic tag rather than a fifth borrowing of a real one.
-- Handled alongside this migration, not left to fail.
--
-- GENERATED by gen599.mjs; the English was never retyped.


-- ---- 433 page strings ------------------------------------------------
